What are Network Types?

A network type tells us how large a network is and where it is used.

Some networks connect just a few devices in one room, while others connect millions of devices across the world.

1. PAN (Personal Area Network)

A PAN is the smallest type of network.

It connects devices around one person, usually within a few meters.

Examples
Mobile ↔ Bluetooth Earbuds
Laptop ↔ Wireless Mouse
Smart Watch ↔ Mobile Phone
Phone
   │
Bluetooth
   │
Earbuds
Range
Around 10 meters
Used For
Personal devices
Bluetooth communication

2. LAN (Local Area Network)

A LAN connects devices within a small area.

Examples:

Home
School
Office
Computer Lab
          Router
        /    |    \
      PC   Laptop  Printer
Characteristics
High speed
Low cost
Easy to manage
Examples
College Computer Lab
Office Network
Home Wi-Fi

3. MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)

A MAN connects multiple LANs within a city.

Example:

A university has 5 campuses in Bengaluru.

Each campus has its own LAN.

All campuses are connected together.

Campus A ---- Campus B
      \        /
       \      /
      Campus C
Used By
Universities
Banks
Government offices

4. WAN (Wide Area Network)

A WAN connects networks across countries or continents.

The biggest WAN is:

The Internet

India
   │
USA
   │
